- If the integer array parameter `nums` is rearranged into the lexicographically next greater permutation of numbers, the integer array result is equal to the rearranged `nums`.
- If the integer array parameter `nums` cannot be rearranged into the lexicographically next greater permutation of numbers, the integer array result is equal to the sorted `nums` in ascending order.
- The length of the integer array `nums` is greater than or equal to 1 and is less than or equal to 100.
- All values in the integer array `nums` are greater than or equal to 0 and are less than or equal to 100.